  "patches": [
    "Ordinary disconnect removes own blur/keydown callbacks; reconnect rebinds once. Permanent host dispose terminates all input/selection/timer entry points; disconnected WiredBase refuses redraw. Twelve original Lit-local listeners may remain on externally retained detached shadow nodes (nine combo event parts and three card slotchange parts), but there is no window/document listener and probes cannot change selection, draw, or schedule timers. No claim of zero listeners on externally retained nodes.",
    "Missing demo root falls back to a visible body alert without installing listeners. Original item press transitions/scale get a prefers-reduced-motion override.",
    "Original three combos and literal options unchanged; original Check console.log replaced by visible local output.",
    "Original rough geometry algorithms retained, no redraw imitation. Host framing and original demo margin/font CSS only.",
    "Explicit disabled and hidden guards for keyboard/pointer; aria-disabled state.",
    "Popup timeout tracking, cancellation on hide/disconnect, one popup pending per component.",
    "WiredCard calls super connect/disconnect, reconnects resize observation, resets removed fallback handler and refuses detached observation.",
    "Host visibility redraw, abortable global listeners, observer disposal, pagehide/atlas:dispose cleanup.",
    "Original Lit performUpdate and deferred popup exceptions report a composed failure to host, which clears scene and shows text alert.",
    "No fonts, images, backend, storage, clipboard, remote network or animation added."
  ],
  "sourceFidelity": "Original example options, Lit components and RoughJS geometry preserved with disclosed lifecycle/disabled/error-boundary compatibility patches. Host is original new framing, not upstream whole site.",
  "nativeGeometryVerified": false,
  "visualVerified": false,
  "browserLimitation": "Chromium launch blocked by environment socket Operation not permitted; no bypass or screenshots. DOM tests use explicit geometry fixtures, not visual proof."
}
